{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cg_premise_violation_is_detectable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cg_premise_violation_is_detectable","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L158-L160","doc":"And that failure is realisable: some choice makes it nonzero over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cg_needs_both_premises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cg_needs_both_premises","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L144-L156","doc":"**Both premises are load-bearing.**  Drop (P2) — let the electromagnetic\nshift differ between the two members of a U-spin multiplet, so that `p` and\n`Σ⁺` carry `a` and `a'` — and the combination no longer vanishes.\n\nStated by exhibiting the failure: with the `Σ⁺` shift changed from `a` to `a'`,\nthe combination becomes `a' − a`, which is nonzero whenever the U-spin premise\nis genuinely violated. So Coleman–Glashow *does* test (P1) ∧ (P2); what it\ncannot do is discriminate among mechanisms that satisfy both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.splittings_not_identically_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.splittings_not_identically_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L137-L142","doc":"The individual splittings are **not** identically zero, so\n`coleman_glashow_identity` is a genuine cancellation among nonzero terms rather\nthan the trivial statement that nothing varies.  Witnessed over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.strong_only_all_splittings_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.strong_only_all_splittings_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L125-L133","doc":"With the electromagnetic shifts switched off, every splitting in the\ncombination vanishes separately — so the relation is not a statement about the\nstrong sector, and is *empty* without electromagnetism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cg_cannot_discriminate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cg_cannot_discriminate","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L112-L121","doc":"**The discriminating-power statement.**  Two arbitrarily different breaking\npatterns — hence arbitrarily different physics — give the same value of the\nColeman–Glashow combination, namely zero.  The relation cannot tell them apart.\n\nThis is the analogue of `GellMannOkuboIdentity.gmo_cannot_discriminate` and\n`DecupletEqualSpacing.equal_spacing_cannot_discriminate`, with the same\nconsequence: reproducing the relation is not evidence for any mechanism. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:u-spin-coleman-glashow","label":"rem:u-spin-coleman-glashow","md":"quantum-observable-universe/eightfold-way/u-spin-coleman-glashow.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.coleman_glashow_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.coleman_glashow_identity","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L101-L110","doc":"**Coleman–Glashow is an identity of the first-order ansatz.**  The\ncombination vanishes for *every* choice of the three strong and three\nelectromagnetic parameters, over any commutative ring.\n\nThe alternating structure is exactly what cancels the U-spin shifts: `a`\nappears in `p` and `Σ⁺` with opposite sign, `b` in `n` and `Ξ⁰`, `c` in `Σ⁻`\nand `Ξ⁻`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cgCombination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.cgCombination","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L95-L99","doc":"The Coleman–Glashow combination. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_XiMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_XiMinus","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_XiZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_XiZero","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_SigMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_SigMinus","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_SigPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_SigPlus","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_n","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.m_p","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ColemanGlashowIdentity.mass","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ColemanGlashowIdentity.lean#L79-L84","doc":"Octet baryon mass under first-order breaking: an isospin-multiplet strong\npart plus a U-spin-multiplet electromagnetic part.\n\n`strong` is the strong contribution shared by an isospin multiplet (P1);\n`em` is the electromagnetic shift shared by a U-spin multiplet (P2). ","signatureChunk":0}]}